URL: https://mirrors.kernel.org/gnu/libtool/libtool-2.4.7.tar.xz 2ea6756908621775a2466f58d79095fb42e6fb6aa599c3a334f3c688781e00e3
URL: https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/libtool/libtool-2.4.7.tar.xz 2ea6756908621775a2466f58d79095fb42e6fb6aa599c3a334f3c688781e00e3
Origname: libtool-2.4.7
Name: libtool

    libtool 2.4.7 (the GNU libtool script + the libltdl shared library).
    The base-system libtool build of the postlc chain (part2) and the
    same-version drop-in rebuild that the postlc12 login-manager stage
    runs (idempotent in a from-scratch chain, the actual libltdl fixer
    for recovery chains that start from pre-fix snapshots).  Everything
    in the chroot that dlopens plugins (libcanberra's dso backend) goes
    through /usr/lib/libltdl.so from this package.
    Fil-C fix (see the patch): ltdl.c declares the never-defined data
    symbol lt_libltdl_LTX_preloaded_symbols extern (it is only ever
    defined inside ltmain-generated convenience libraries that link
    ltdl statically) and references it from lt_dlinit's HAVE_LIBDLLOADER
    block; the fil-C compiler routes that reference through a
    pizlonated_ forwarder, so the built /usr/lib/libltdl.so carries a
    NON-WEAK undefined reference to pizlonated_lt_libltdl_LTX_preloaded_
    symbols, which poisons every -lltdl link of an executable and every
    runtime load.  Declaring the reference weak makes it resolve to
    NULL -- lt_dlpreload(NULL) is the documented "clear the preloaded
    list" path (loaders/preopen.c guards the NULL and falls back to its
    own default_preloaded_symbols) -- so the standalone library's
    behavior is unchanged and the builtin loader vtable still gets
    installed.  This patch was previously checked in as the side file
    pizlix/libtool-2.4.7-filc-ltdl-1.patch; it now lives here.
diff --git a/libtool/libltdl/ltdl.c b/libtool/libltdl/ltdl.c
--- a/libtool/libltdl/ltdl.c
+++ b/libtool/libltdl/ltdl.c
@@ -218,7 +218,15 @@
 LT_SCOPE const lt_dlvtable *	get_vtable (lt_user_data data);
 LT_END_C_DECLS
 #ifdef HAVE_LIBDLLOADER
-extern LT_DLSYM_CONST lt_dlsymlist preloaded_symbols[];
+/* Fil-C: this list is only ever DEFINED inside ltmain-generated
+   convenience libraries that link ltdl statically; the standalone
+   libltdl build has always shipped an undefined reference here.  The
+   fil-C compiler routes the reference through a pizlonated_ forwarder,
+   which made the shared library unshippable (a hard undefined symbol
+   poisons every executable link and every load).  Declare it weak: the
+   reference then resolves to NULL, which is exactly what lt_dlpreload
+   (loaders/preopen.c) already handles -- "clear the preloaded list".  */
+extern LT_DLSYM_CONST lt_dlsymlist preloaded_symbols[] __attribute__((__weak__));
 #endif

 /* Initialize libltdl. */
